{"key": "0433fb04da44c6c8634ed2650c2f3d5883ddde74b70afafa640be67254bff3e9", "value": {"response": "```python\ndef add(lst):\n    \"\"\"Given a non-empty list of integers lst. add the even elements that are at odd indices.\n    \n    Examples:\n        add([4, 2, 6, 7]) ==> 2 \n    \"\"\"\n    return sum(num for i, num in enumerate(lst) if i % 2 != 0 and num % 2 == 0)\n```", "prompt_eval_count": 805, "eval_count": 83}}
{"key": "c4242707dd685da26c5553647c84f7cbdd69a15797655b6b4e22900346ac8c7e", "value": {"response": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef iscube(a):\n    '''\n    Write a function that takes an integer a and returns True \n    if this ingeger is a cube of some integer number.\n    Note: you may assume the input is always valid.\n    Examples:\n    iscube(1) ==> True\n    iscube(2) ==> False\n    iscube(-1) ==> True\n    iscube(64) ==> True\n    iscube(0) ==> True\n    iscube(180) ==> False\n    '''\n    # Check if the number is a perfect cube\n    root = round(a ** (1. / 3))\n    return root ** 3 == a\n\n# Test the function\nprint(iscube(1))   # True\nprint(iscube(2))   # False\nprint(iscube(-1))  # True\nprint(iscube(64))  # True\nprint(iscube(0))   # True\nprint(iscube(180)) # False\n```", "prompt_eval_count": 870, "eval_count": 209}}
